Changelog: 09-10-2026 17:51:51

tools/tests/test_instance_copies.py: the copies of bc250_core's instance module in the apps not yet on core
must match it (only the SPDX line may differ).

Changelog: 09-10-2026 16:28:35

New app: apps/system-overlay (BC-250 System Overlay), a small always-on-top window with CPU, GPU, refresh
rate, fan and temperatures. Added to the README, the docs, the bug report form and CLAUDE.md; CI runs its
tests, a new installer test (tools/installer-tests/system-overlay.sh) and warning-level shellcheck on its
install.sh. The README's list of apps in /opt now includes persistent-acpi.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 16:10:58

images/bc250-bazzite-suite.png added at the repository root: the suite icon, the same file as the portal's
portal/images/bc250-bazzite-suite.png.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 13:56:58

CI: a new installer test, tools/installer-tests/persistent-acpi.sh, and warning-level shellcheck for
persistent-acpi's scripts. The root requirements-dev.txt includes persistent-acpi's test requirements.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 13:24:51

tools/check_versions.py prints a one-line summary when every version matches, instead of nothing.
A mismatch is reported as before, and the exit codes are unchanged.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 12:15:17

install.sh in the repository root installs the suite from the checkout, for testing: it runs portal/install.sh
with the same options. CI's bash -n and shellcheck passes include it, and the portal installer test goes
through it.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 11:51:07

Installer tests: the shims point BC250_LOG_DIR into the test folder, so the purge step no longer reaches the
board's real /var/log/bc250-bazzite-test. portal.sh now checks that purge removes bazzite-test's results.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 11:44:51

Local checks now match CI, including the shellcheck error and bash -n passes and check_manifest's --base;
changelog times are CEST on both systems; the commands to create the development venv on each system.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 11:20:42

READMEs and the manual describe only what exists: migration status, plans and decisions moved to MIGRATION.md,
which neither links to. Removed the empty placeholder folders lib/sh and tools/i18n. The portal README's
development command now uses the development venv, since Bazzite's own python3 has no PyQt6.

Changelog: 08-10-2026 22:35:00

Suite-wide changes: the repository, CI, release tooling and the shared code. Each app, core/ and portal/ keep
their own CHANGELOG for their own changes; this file covers what is not part of any one of them.

Migration step 3: the portal and the release tooling.
- Releases: one per tag, <app>-v<x.y.z> or portal-v<x.y.z>, built by .github/workflows/release.yml with
  tools/build_release.py. Each release is a reproducible <tag>.tar.gz plus SHA256SUMS. A portal release bundles
  the bazzite-test release it pins.
- portal/apps.toml pins one release of every app. tools/pin_app.py records a released app's tag and checksum;
  tools/check_manifest.py (CI) requires every app to be listed and a portal version bump at least as large as
  the largest app bump it pins.
- tools/stage_app.py builds an app's install tree. Each app ships the bc250_core it was tested with.
- tools/installer-tests/ run the portal and bazzite-test installers and the release flow end to end on Linux
  without root (fakeroot); they run in CI.
- CI: the portal manifest rule, tests for core, portal, tools and bazzite-test, shellcheck at warning level for
  the suite's own scripts, and the installer tests.

Migration step 2: bc250_core, the code the apps share (see core/CHANGELOG).

Migration step 1: the suite repository.
- The seven apps moved in under apps/, each with its own VERSION (all 0.1.0), LICENSE, .gitignore and
  CHANGELOG. Their old per-repo GitHub workflows were removed in favour of the root .github/.
- LF line endings everywhere, also on Windows (.gitattributes). Scripts are executable in git
  (tools/fix-modes.sh, checked in CI).
- tools/check_versions.py (CI) keeps every hard-coded version equal to its VERSION file.
- test.sh runs all test suites, with one venv per OS (.venv-linux, .venv-windows).
- MkDocs manual skeleton in docs/, built with --strict in CI.
